<title>UK: UK natural gas output soared by 18.5 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>UK natural gas output soared by 18.5 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British natural gas output rose by 18.5 percent to a new record in 1996 ,the Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) said in a provisional study on Thursday.</p>
<p>Electricity generation also rose, by five percent, last year, the DTI said.</p>
<p>Oil production was steady and coal production fell by four percent, the DTI said.</p>
<p>The DTI said total energy production increased by five percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
